- op: discuss  # 8a9a
  at: '2026-09-29T03:07:55Z'  # 8a9a
  by: agent  # 8a9a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8a9a
  clock: 3  # 8a9a
  nonce: 8a9a  # 8a9a
  message: "SATISFIED -- DONE AND NEVER CLOSED. Fixed by INV-midag (916bc980b5, 2026-09-24, PR #1180: \"a call is anchored to the function that contains it\", c/rust/ruby/csharp), which replaced the name-keyed enclosing lookup with a position lookup. That is the root cause this item left NOT ESTABLISHED: the lookup was name-keyed by construction (last writer wins), not a bypassed span test.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-verified 2026-09-28 on dev 51c73cce78:\n- The item's own repro (two cfg-gated fn ts(), calls in the first): all three calls (now, elapsed, as_secs) have src rust:src/main.rs:2-5:ts:function. The same repro on pinned worktrees: 916bc980b5^ -> src 8-8:ts (the defect), 916bc980b5 -> src 2-5:ts. So the move is that commit's.\n- The live instance, loro crates/loro-internal/src/change.rs: the host_info_read std::time::SystemTime.now chain is anchored on 288-295:get_sys_timestamp (the non-wasm variant that makes the call), no longer on 300-311.\n- Variants the repro did not cover: the twins in reverse order (calls in the second) -> correct; two cfg(unix)/cfg(windows) impl methods S.run -> the call is on the unix one (13-13); the C #ifdef/#else analogue the item flagged as unchecked (two int ts(void), calls in the #else one) -> all calls on the right twin (8-10).\nScope: rust and c checked here; INV-midag's own evidence covers the other languages it fixed.\n\nSEEN IN PASSING, NOT THIS ITEM: loro's wasm variant calls its own wasm_bindgen extern `fn now()` (JS Date.now), and the chain names std::time::Instant.now: a bare unresolved `now` matched a catalogue row by name. The boundary (host_info_read) is right for a clock read; the primitive name is wrong. Not filed."  # 8a9a
